From 318d5119ca9521107d6e4fabaf3fb9bb32f6a699 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 17:05:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(serve): forge serve MVP -- interactive local dashboard

Add `forge serve [--port N] [--open]`: a loopback-only companion that turns
the static dashboard into an interactive one. The browser never mutates the
kernel directly -- it POSTs the SAME forge verbs the CLI/agents use to
/api/mutation, which relays them IN-PROCESS through the existing command
dispatch (resolveCommandOpts + executeCommand). All validation stays in the
verb/broker handlers; the server adds no parallel validator and never spawns
an agent.

Endpoints: GET /health (capability probe), GET /data.json (baked snapshot,
background-refreshed; a mutation regenerates before responding), POST
/api/mutation ({token,verb,args}). Verbs: issue.create/update/close/comment
(-> broker commitGuardedAccept) + gate + role.

Security: binds 127.0.0.1 only; per-run random token injected into the served
page URL fragment and REQUIRED on every POST (constant-time compare); POST
rejects non-loopback Host / foreign Origin (CSRF fence); token dies with the
process, no accounts/cloud/daemon.

Dashboard (web/dashboard/app.js) uses the DataSource seam to flip
SNAPSHOT->LIVE on /health: Add-issue modal, per-issue status/priority/close/
comment controls, and a Controls panel that RUNs gate/role while still
offering copy. Degrades to read + copy-as-command on file:// or no server.

Tested without leaving a server hanging: in-process handler routing (verb
allowlist, real gate/role rejection + success) plus one bounded server smoke
on port 0 that closes in afterEach. serve.js passes sonarjs cognitive-
complexity < 15; ESLint --max-warnings 0 clean.

